{"step_index":36,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:41:52Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-17T12:11:52+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T12:11:54+05:30\nCreated At: 2026-11-17T12:11:52+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T12:11:54+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n# Reward policy decisions\r\n\r\nThis is a working register from the supplied Kezza implementation brief and product guide. These values must remain server-controlled and versioned.\r\n\r\n## Working rules from the supplied specification\r\n\r\n- Three-month reward cycle.\r\n- ₹1,00,000 minimum eligible collected sales per cycle.\r\n- One point per whole rupee of eligible amount approved by an authorized reviewer; fractional rupees are rounded down unless finance approves another integer rule.\r\n- Ten points have an indicative value of ₹1. That is a preview only; it is not a cash promise or treatment-credit promise.\r\n- Points are not credited on a submitted or pending claim. Each credit must follow a verified approval and be traceable to a source payment.\r\n- Reversals, expiry and corrections append ledger entries; they never erase the original.\r\n- Recruitment commissions are separate and disabled for this MVP unless Kezza explicitly re-approves them.\r\n\r\n## Kezza approval is still required\r\n\r\n1. Reward delivery: cash, Kezza treatment credit, or hybrid.\r\n2. Cycle calendar and exact dates: fixed quarters or rolling/custom three-month windows.\r\n3. How late approvals are handled: include them in the original cycle, approve without reward eligibility, or reject them. The current `approve_no_points` option excludes late-approved sales from both points and threshold eligibility; Kezza must confirm this interpretation before approval.\r\n4. Whether threshold qualification applies to all cycle points or only a qualifying subset. The API requires this choice in each approved policy.\r\n5. Net eligible sales definition for discounts, tax, packages, deposits, split payments, cancellations and refunds.\r\n6. Refund/reversal treatment after a cycle has closed and handling of a negative balance. The current API blocks reversal after close until this rule is defined.\r\n7. Whether unused points expire after close/settlement and the exact expiry timing. The current API requires explicit expiry approval and waits until no eligible or approved settlement remains.\r\n8. Patient referral ownership rules for existing patients, repeat visits, attribution expiry and cross-agent duplicates.\r\n9. Exact patient-consent and privacy wording, retention and support process.\r\n10. Google OAuth, SMS/WhatsApp, push and private file-storage provider credentials/configuration.\r\n\r\nUntil the applicable approvals exist, the API exposes preview data and refuses policy approval, reward awards, and cycle close where a required choice is missing. Cycle expiry is a separate explicit action after close and settlement processing. There is no default password, fake account, patient, invoice, sale, reward, or admin credential.\r\n"}
{"step_index":37,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:41:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-17T12:11:53+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T12:11:54+05:30\nCreated At: 2026-11-17T12:11:53+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-17T12:11:54+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n# Kezza Agent Rewards: API and integration guide\r\n\r\nAll API routes are mounted below `/api/v1`. The API owns identity, permissions, consent records, referral attribution, payment review, reward policy, points ledger, and audit records. Mobile and admin clients never connect directly to PostgreSQL.\r\n\r\n## Agent API flow\r\n\r\n| Workflow | Endpoint | Result |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Request OTP | `POST /auth/otp/request` | Sends an OTP request; local development returns `dev_code` only when mock OTP is enabled. |\r\n| Verify OTP | `POST /auth/otp/verify` | Existing active user receives a session; an invited agent receives a short lived phone-verification token. |\r\n| Activate invite | `POST /auth/agent/activate` | Requires verified phone and a one-time administrator invitation code. |\r\n| Read dashboard/profile | `GET /agent/dashboard`, `GET /agent/profile` | Returns server-side referral and points summary. |\r\n| Read referral list/detail | `GET /agent/referrals`, `GET /agent/referrals/{id}` | Returns only referrals attributed to the signed-in agent. |\r\n| Create referral | `POST /agent/referrals` | Requires active consent document/version and an idempotency key. Consent text is not invented by the app. |\r\n| Update referral status | `PATCH /agent/referrals/{id}/status` | Restricts agent changes to permitted non-final workflow statuses. |\r\n| Create payment claim | `POST /agent/payments/claims` | Creates/reuses an invoice and submits a claimed collection; invoice totals and prior claims are checked. |\r\n| Upload receipt | `POST /agent/payments/claims/{id}/evidence` | Private JPEG, PNG, or PDF evidence, maximum 8 MB. |\r\n| Respond to reviewer | `POST /agent/payments/claims/{id}/respond` | Resubmits a claim waiting for additional information. |\r\n| Read wallet | `GET /agent/wallet` | Returns server ledger balance, entries, and a clearly labelled indicative estimate. |\r\n| Read branches/services/legal docs | `/agent/branches`, `/agent/services`, `/agent/legal-documents` | Returns active, server-managed catalog items and approved documents. |\r\n| Record document acceptance | `POST /agent/legal-documents/{id}/accept` | Stores accepted document ID/version and server timestamp. |\r\n| Feedback/branch change/notifications | `/agent/feedback`, `/agent/branch-change-requests`, `/agent/notifications` | Submits and reads operational requests and notifications. |\r\n\r\nAfter login, native mobile stores its refresh session in Expo Secure Store. The admin web portal keeps the short lived access token in memory and uses the API's HTTP-only refresh cookie. Sensitive API operations still verify role, branch scope, and record ownership on the server.\r\n\r\n## Admin responsibilities\r\n\r\nThe admin portal exposes agent invitations, scoped staff accounts, payment review, branch and service catalogs, reward policies and cycle preview/close, settlement review, branch-change decisions, feedback, legal document versioning, release notes, audit history, and a reward ledger CSV.\r\n\r\n- Branch reviewers may inspect scoped work and request more information or reject claims.\r\n- Finance reviewers and super-admins can approve collected payment claims; self-approval is denied.\r\n- Operations admins manage permitted operational setup; super-admins handle high impact approval actions.\r\n- Policy/document/release approval requires a different super-admin from the creator where the API enforces dual control.\r\n- Every sensitive decision records an actor, reason, and audit event.\r\n\r\n## Money and reward handling\r\n\r\nMoney is stored as integer paise. An invoice may have multiple partial collection claims, but the sum of reserved and approved claims cannot exceed the invoice amount. A claim cannot award points while pending. Finance approval appends integer point credits according to the approved policy and cycle. Refunds/reversals append ledger entries; existing entries are not overwritten. Settlement and expiry actions append ledger events with idempotency keys.\r\n\r\nThe current working policy is 1 point per eligible whole rupee, 10 points per indicative ₹1, and a ₹1,00,000 cycle threshold. Whether points accrue on every eligible rupee or only above the threshold is an unselected policy decision. Payout method, exact dates, late approvals, and refund handling also require Kezza approval. The API blocks use of policies with unresolved required choices.\r\n\r\n## Isolated database and evidence\r\n\r\nUse only the dedicated `kezza_rewards_db` database for this code. Alembic checks the configured URL and live PostgreSQL database name before migrating; `/health/db` reports healthy only when the connected database name matches. The initial migration creates 25 tables and seeds only the three listed Kezza branch records. It does not seed users, patients, invoices, payments, reward balances, or admin credentials.\r\n\r\nReceipts are stored outside the public web directory and downloaded only after API authorization. The local filesystem backend is a development setup; production should use private object storage with lifecycle/retention policy and audit logging.\r\n\r\n## Local development notes\r\n\r\n- Set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` to `<base>/api/v1`; for a phone on Wi-Fi use the Mac LAN IP, not `localhost`.\r\n- Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` to the same API base. The API CORS list must include the admin origin and any Expo web origin used for development.\r\n- `OTP_PROVIDER=mock` is for development only. The implementation returns the OTP only in development and applies basic resend, attempt, phone, and IP limits. Use an approved SMS service and operational rate limits before public exposure.\r\n- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS` can be configured for optional server-verified Google account linking; the agent must already be invited and active.\r\n- Add the active patient consent document through the admin portal using exact Kezza-approved wording before agents can submit patient referrals.\r\n\r\nFor database bootstrap and run commands, follow [`setup-macos.md`](setup-macos.md).\r\n"}
{"step_index":38,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:41:54Z","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","input_tokens":3313,"cache_read_tokens":64170,"output_tokens":1908,"content":"Excellent context. I now have everything needed. Let me create the SPEC + ROADMAP and then kick off the phased execution using swarm.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# SPEC.md — Kezza Agent Rewards Platform\n**Status: FINALIZED**\n**Last Updated: 2026-11-17**\n\n---\n\n## Product Overview\n\nKezza Agent Rewards is an invitation-only mobile-first referral platform for Kezza clinic agents. Agents refer patients, submit collected-payment claims, and earn reward points after authorized finance review. No self-registration. No client-side balance editing.\n\n---\n\n## Stack (Locked)\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|---|---|\n| Mobile | Expo SDK 57, React Native 0.86.3, Expo Router, TanStack Query v5, Zustand, Axios, Secure Store |\n| Backend | Python 3.11+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, PostgreSQL (`kezza_rewards_db`) |\n| Admin | Next.js App Router, TypeScript, React |\n| Auth | JWT access tokens (mobile: Secure Store) + rotated refresh sessions (admin: HTTP-only cookie) |\n\n---\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1: Identity & Invitation\n- FR-1.1 Admin creates invitation tied to a branch + phone + agent_code (expires 72h)\n- FR-1.2 Agent requests OTP for their mobile number\n- FR-1.3 OTP verified → existing active user gets full session; invited user gets phone-verify token\n- FR-1.4 Agent activates invite using phone-verify token + invitation code → creates User record → full session\n- FR-1.5 Open self-registration is disabled\n- FR-1.6 Refresh token rotation on every use; revoked on sign-out\n\n### FR-2: Patient Referral\n- FR-2.1 Agent adds patient: name, phone (unique), service, branch attribution, note\n- FR-2.2 Must display and confirm active approved consent text (version + timestamp stored)\n- FR-2.3 Idempotency key prevents duplicate referral on retry\n- FR-2.4 Referral status flow: new → contacted → in_progress → converted | not_converted | closed\n- FR-2.5 Agent can only view/update their own referrals\n- FR-2.6 Patient phone is unique across the system\n\n### FR-3: Payment Claims\n- FR-3.1 Agent selects a referral, enters invoice number, invoice amount, collected amount, date, method, transaction ref\n- FR-3.2 Invoice number unique per branch (normalized)\n- FR-3.3 Multiple partial claims per invoice allowed; sum of reserved+approved ≤ invoice amount\n- FR-3.4 Agent uploads receipt evidence (JPEG/PNG/PDF, max 8MB); stored outside public dir\n- FR-3.5 Claim status: draft → submitted → under_review → needs_information → resubmitted → approved | rejected | reversed\n- FR-3.6 Agent responds to needs_information with additional note → resubmitted\n- FR-3.7 Agent cannot approve own claim\n\n### FR-4: Payment Review (Admin)\n- FR-4.1 Branch reviewer: inspect claims in their branch scope, return for info, reject\n- FR-4.2 Finance reviewer: approve with approved_amount_paise, return for info, reject\n- FR-4.3 Self-approval denied (reviewer_id ≠ agent_id)\n- FR-4.4 All decisions recorded in payment_decisions with reason + idempotency key\n- FR-4.5 On approval: points credited to reward_ledger per active approved policy\n\n### FR-5: Reward Points & Cycles\n- FR-5.1 Working policy: 1 pt per whole eligible rupee, 10 pts = ₹1 indicative\n- FR-5.2 Three-month cycle, ₹1,00,000 threshold minimum\n- FR-5.3 Points credited only after approved claim, never on pending\n- FR-5.4 Ledger append-only: credit, reversal, expiry, settlement, adjustment entry_types\n- FR-5.5 Cycle states: scheduled → open → closing → closed\n- FR-5.6 Admin previews cycle before close; close action guarded by policy completion\n- FR-5.7 Settlements generated on close; external payment ref recorded after payout\n\n### FR-6: Mobile Screens (Complete States)\nEvery screen must have: loading, error/retry, empty, and populated states.\n\n| Screen | Must Have |\n|---|---|\n| Login | Phone input + OTP request; dev_code display in dev mode |\n| OTP Verify | 6-digit input, resend, error states |\n| Activate | Full name, invitation code entry, validation |\n| Home/Overview | Stats row, agent code card, cycle progress bar, quick actions, recent referrals |\n| Patients tab | Searchable list, status filter, pull-to-refresh |\n| Referral detail | Status + history, linked claims, update status action |\n| Add patient | Consent display + confirm checkbox, all fields validated |\n| Payments tab | Claims list with status badges, pull-to-refresh |\n| Payment claim detail | Evidence upload, reviewer feedback, respond action |\n| Add payment | Referral picker, invoice fields, amount validation |\n| Wallet/Rewards | Points balance, ledger list, cycle progress, indicative value |\n| Profile | Agent info, branch, sign-out, links to secondary screens |\n| Notifications | List with mark-read, unread count badge |\n| Branches | Branch directory with phone/maps links |\n| Feedback | Category, message, rating, contact permission |\n| Policies | Active legal docs, acceptance recording |\n\n### FR-7: Admin Portal (All Panels Complete)\n| Panel | Required Operations |\n|---|---|\n| Overview | Operational counts, pending queues by branch |\n| Agents | Create invitation, list agents, suspend/reactivate |\n| Payment Review | Inspect claim + evidence, approve/return/reject with reason |\n| Rewards & Cycles | Policy CRUD, cycle create/preview/close, settlement review |\n| Branches & Services | Branch CRUD, service catalog, branch-change decisions |\n| Feedback | View + respond to agent feedback |\n| Documents & Audit | Legal doc versioning, app releases, audit log search |\n\n### FR-8: Non-Functional\n- FR-8.1 All money stored as integer paise\n- FR-8.2 Audit log on every sensitive action (actor, action, entity, before/after JSON)\n- FR-8.3 JWT expiry 15min access / 7-day refresh session\n- FR-8.4 OTP: 6 digits, 10-minute expiry, max 5 attempts, rate-limited by phone+IP\n- FR-8.5 TypeScript strict, no `any`; Python typed with Pydantic v2\n- FR-8.6 DB: `kezza_rewards_db` only; health endpoint rejects wrong DB name\n- FR-8.7 Receipt files: private storage, served only after auth check\n- FR-8.8 CORS: only configured origins\n\n---\n\n## Out of Scope (MVP)\n- Recruitment commissions (disabled)\n- Push notifications (in-app only)\n- SMS provider integration (mock OTP in dev; placeholder for prod)\n- Google OAuth (schema ready, not wired in MVP)\n- Production receipt storage (local filesystem in dev)\n- Multi-currency or non-INR support\n","Path":"/Users/ravi/.codex/.chatgpt-projects/g-p-6ae81da483248191a7e1c68af4392bce/kezza-agent-app 2/.gsd/SPEC.md"}}]}
